# Listed so that anyone who finds the earlier version first is told it is
# superseded, rather than citing it and attributing to this work two claims it
# withdraws.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Rate-Distortion Function for Model Merging"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Pathak"
        given-names: "Sankalp"
      - family-names: "Garg"
        given-names: "Sanjay"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21238820"
    notes: "Superseded earlier version of this work, posted as a preprint. It
      presents as headline results two claims the manuscript above does not
      make: that the rate-distortion bound is the contribution, and that the
      authors' encoder attains the lowest worst-task loss on all four bases at
      default hyperparameters. Where the two documents disagree, the manuscript
      above is current."
